# 6. Privacy Policy Analysis

## Aim

To compare the privacy policies of different technology companies and understand how they collect, use, share, retain, protect, and delete users' personal data.

## Introduction

A privacy policy explains how an organization handles personal information collected from its users. It generally describes the types of data collected, the purpose of collection, third-party sharing, data retention, cookies and tracking, security measures, user rights, and procedures for deleting personal information.

For this study, the privacy policies of **Google, Apple, and Microsoft** are compared. These companies provide widely used digital services and therefore handle different types of personal and technical information.

## Objectives

1. To identify the types of personal data collected by companies.
2. To understand why personal information is collected.
3. To examine third-party data sharing.
4. To study data retention and deletion practices.
5. To understand user privacy rights.
6. To examine cookies and tracking technologies.
7. To identify privacy gaps and suggest improvements.

